    "body": "Both build systems build `ctime_tests` without running it as part of the standard test suite. This change registers constant-time test execution in both CTest and Autotools `make check`.\n\nWhen MemorySanitizer is enabled, the test executes directly; under Valgrind builds, it runs under `valgrind --error-exitcode=42`. For Valgrind configurations, registration is cleanly omitted with a configure notice if the binary is absent or during cross-compilation. The Autotools integration employs a dedicated runner to prevent a global `LOG_COMPILER` from wrapping Valgrind twice, allowing the standalone CI invocation in `ci/ci.sh` to be retired.\n\nVerification covers both CMake and Autotools suites under standard, MSan, and Valgrind configurations, confirming that deliberate branching on poisoned secrets triggers test failure while clean trees pass.\n\nAddresses #1560.\n",
